.TH tugantt n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tugantt
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBgantt\fR block and renders it natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine. A self\-contained 2D renderer in the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR family (like \fBtupie\fR / \fBtusankey\fR); normally you call \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR / \fBtuflow::toPng\fR, which dispatch here.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tugantt 0.3
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tugantt::parse text                           ;# -> gantt model dict
::tclutils::tugantt::toSvg  model ?-width W? ?-height H? ?-fontfile f? ?-scale n?
::tclutils::tugantt::toPng  model ?...?                   ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tugantt::writeSvg model file ?...?
::tclutils::tugantt::writePng model file ?...?
.CE
.PP
\fBwriteSvg\fR and \fBwritePng\fR write through a temporary file (\fBcommon::replaceFile\fR): a failed write leaves the old file and no open channel (tclutils 0.69.0).
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
gantt
  title <text>                 optional chart title
  dateFormat <fmt>             input date format (default YYYY-MM-DD)
  axisFormat <fmt>             optional axis label format
  section <name>               start a labelled group of tasks
  <title> : [tags,] [id,] <start>, <end-or-duration>
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fBTags\fR (optional, must come first): \fBactive\fR, \fBdone\fR, \fBcrit\fR, \fBmilestone\fR. They set the bar colour; a \fBmilestone\fR is drawn as a diamond.
.IP \(bu
\fBStart\fR: an explicit date, \fBafter <id> [<id> ...]\fR (the latest end of the referenced tasks), or omitted — the task then starts at the end of the preceding task. The first task needs a start: if it has no date and no \fBafter\fR that names an earlier task, drawing raises \fB{TCLUTILS TUGANTT DATE}\fR (Mermaid, too, needs a start date; there is no fallback to 1970 or today).
.IP \(bu
\fBDates\fR must exist: the parsed date is formatted back with the same format and compared with the input (leading zeros do not matter, \fB2026\-3\-2\fR is fine). \fB2026\-13\-45\fR or \fB2026\-02\-30\fR raise \fBDATE\fR on Tcl 8.6 and 9.0 alike.
.IP \(bu
\fBEnd\fR: an explicit date, or a duration \fB5d\fR / \fB2w\fR / \fB8h\fR / \fB30m\fR / \fB10s\fR / \fB500ms\fR. Another unit (\fB5x\fR) raises \fBDURATION\fR (0.3; 0.2 made it a task of length 0).
.IP \(bu
\fBIds\fR may hold letters of any script (\fBbüro\fR; 0.2 took such an id for the start date and failed on the whole chart).
.IP \(bu
\fBdateFormat\fR / \fBaxisFormat\fR accept the usual tokens \fBYYYY MM DD HH mm ss\fR (mapped to \fBclock\fR format); \fBX\fR means a Unix timestamp.
.IP \(bu
\fBAxis\fR: about six ticks, snapped to whole units of the axis format (seconds if it shows seconds, minutes if it shows minutes, hours if it shows hours, otherwise days); a tick whose label repeats the previous one is dropped, so a short span shows each date once.
.IP \(bu
Comments start with \fB%%\fR.
.SS "v1 scope"
.PP
Covered: title, dateFormat/axisFormat, sections, tags, ids, explicit dates, \fBafter\fR dependencies, durations, and milestones. \fBNot\fR in v1: \fBexcludes\fR / weekend exclusion, \fBuntil\fR, \fBvert\fR markers, compact display mode, and custom \fBtickInterval\fR. Without \fB\-height\fR the chart grows with the number of tasks (at least 400 pixels); with \fB\-height\fR the height is fixed and tasks fill from the top.
.SS Options
.PP
\fB\-width\fR (default 800) / \fB\-height\fR (default 0 = automatic: 400, or more when the title, the task rows and the axis labels need it \-\- each task row takes 26 pixels), \fB\-fontfile\fR (a TTF for real\-font labels via \fBGlyphs\fR; PNG only \-\- otherwise the built\-in bitmap font), \fB\-scale\fR (positive integer; on PNG the canvas grows by the factor; on SVG the canvas keeps its size and text, lines and spacing grow by the factor).
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tugantt
set src {gantt
  title Project Plan
  dateFormat YYYY-MM-DD
  section Planning
  Requirements :done, req, 2014-01-01, 4d
  Design       :done, des, after req, 5d
  section Development
  Frontend     :active, fe, after des, 8d
  Backend      :crit, be, after des, 10d
  section Release
  Testing      :test, after be, 4d
  Launch       :milestone, m1, after test, 0d}
::tclutils::tugantt::writePng [::tclutils::tugantt::parse $src] plan.png -scale 2
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR (canvas), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.IP \(bu
Bars use rect primitives and milestones a polygon, so SVG and PNG stay congruent. Bar colours: normal blue, \fBactive\fR light blue, \fBdone\fR grey, \fBcrit\fR red, \fBmilestone\fR amber.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUGANTT <REASON>}\fR \-\- \fBEMPTY\fR (no tasks), \fBARG\fR (bad \fB\-scale\fR), \fBDATE\fR (a date that does not match \fBdateFormat\fR or does not exist, or a first task without a start date \-\- raised when drawing, not by \fBparse\fR), \fBDURATION\fR (a duration with an unknown unit, also raised when drawing), \fBFONT\fR (font file not found).
